          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T03:59:47.988Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes. It's the place helpers Python's core never got (25 of them, listed in <code>not_ported_yet.json5</code> since epic data J10), plus a Python side for each kind of place. Planned as <a href=\"#p33\">P33 · Places in Python</a>, about 4-6h; its plan waits for your Accept.</p>\n<ul><li>JSON folder and CSV file on the server: through the page server's same routes.</li><li>Atmosphere: its HTTP API, as the JS one uses.</li><li>\"a database on this device\": a JSON file beside the program, since a Python program runs on a machine, not in a browser tab.</li></ul>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-07T04:00:17.222Z",
          "text": "send this over to `data` epic"
        },
